From 5dcef6cde7922b469ac3ff6834c5594195d4c14b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:48:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] x86_64/fpu/587: generic ldouble acosh, atanh, asinh,
 cbrt, frexp, cexp

Intel's x87 versions fail math/test-ldouble-* (missing invalid for sNaN,
underflow, accuracy); x86_64 uses the ldbl-96 C code for these, which
runs in the x87 precision anyway.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
